{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors","id":558701,"title":"Spirit Doors.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-17T14:17:00-07:00","id":558701,"title":"Spirit Doors.","content":"How does one calculate social doors for spirits? I thought I saw it somewhere once, but I've been unable to find it ever since.<br /> <br /> Another question re: Social Maneuvering, are rolls to open doors always contested?<br /> <br /> And can spirits still learn/have gifts/facets. I assume they can have them, if they can teach them. Power and finesse like any numina? That makes the most sense, but then what about the ones that scale on renown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T15:05:24-07:00","id":558779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors#post558701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one calculate social doors for spirits? I thought I saw it somewhere once, but I've been unable to find it ever since.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't see a specific rule for it anywhere - the Gathra section is relevant here, but doesn't mention numbers of Doors. Since usually it's lower of Resolve or Composure, I'd go with spirits having Resistance in Doors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another question re: Social Maneuvering, are rolls to open doors always contested? </div> </div> </div>Well if someone *wants* to do something that you want them to do, there's not really any need for Social Manouevering in the first place, I believe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And can spirits still learn/have gifts/facets. I assume they can have them, if they can teach them. Power and finesse like any numina? That makes the most sense, but then what about the ones that scale on renown? </div> </div> </div>No, spirits cannot learn or use Gifts or Facets. They do not teach Gifts - they tear the symbols of those Gifts into the Essence of a werewolf.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T15:18:42-07:00","id":558795,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your answers. I figured I would just use Resistance if I couldn't find anything. I was just so sure that I had seen rules for it once. That's just going to be pretty rough in the case of some spirits. Maybe I'll make it the lower of Finesse or Resistance, because 10 doors on a rank 3 spirits seems a bit much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=558779#post558779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if someone *wants* to do something that you want them to do, there's not really any need for Social Manouevering in the first place, I believe.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>On this though... what if the person doesn't really care too much? Like, if a PC were to try to convince me to let him cut ahead of me in line, am I going to roll my Resolve + Composure to oppose that? That seems a bit extreme. I feel like something like isn't necessarily resisted, and assuming the person asking doesn't creep me out or is even moderately polite (and I'm not pressed for time/in a mood) I'm likely to oblige. Isn't the number of doors itself already representative of the person's resistance to social maneuvers?<br /> <br /> I feel the need to qualify that I wouldn't let them jump me if they weren't already in line behind me.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if that's not the case, then the social doors system to me seems like it's just littered with contested, extended rolls, which are the hardest kind of roll to succeed at. That would mean that being a social character is necessarily and unavoidably the most difficult kind of character to play. Not to mention the creativity necessary at time to make it all work. If I were playing a thief and <i>every</i> larceny roll was extended and contested (and my larceny skill dots were split between 4 or more different skills) I'd have a really hard time being effective, I feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T15:44:56-07:00","id":558809,"title":"","content":"Ah, sorry, I misunderstoof what you were getting at.<br /> <br /> No, rolls to open Doors are not always contested. The Opening Doors section on p.164 covers this - &quot;The Storyteller should present situations that demonstrate the range of possible options, mixing up the dice pools involved. In some cases, she might make the roll into a contested action&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:02:44-07:00","id":559337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=558779#post558779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, spirits cannot learn or use Gifts or Facets. They do not teach Gifts - they tear the symbols of those Gifts into the Essence of a werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't they have numina that works pretty much like the described gifts, tho?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:15:47-07:00","id":559345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=559337#post559337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't they have numina that works pretty much like the described gifts, tho?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily, no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Me, at the beginning of the the Gifts rules in Werewolf 2e</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite their source, Gifts are not alien powers grafted onto the soul of a werewolf. They undeniably reflect the nature of the Uratha as predators. The power of these symbols shines through the lens of the werewolf\u2019s spirit to cast a shadow suited to the hunt and the kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T08:28:45-07:00","id":559399,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there were supposed to be numina that acted like gifts in first edition, but back then gifts were just spirit magic. Now they're an Uratha thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T05:03:39-07:00","id":564006,"title":"","content":"I would still be okay, as a Storyteller, with giving spirits Numina that mirror certain Facets of Shadow Gifts, especially if the spirit resonates with the theme of the Gift. The spirit of a library or a research spirit could definitely have a numen that mirrors <i>Sift the Sands</i> (Wisdom/Knowledge), for example. Or a secrecy spirit who has a numen that mirrors <i>Needle</i> (Cunning/Knowledge). It's not the Facets themselves, but it's not hard to see how they can be translated to suitable numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T20:02:20-07:00","id":572115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=564006#post564006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would still be okay, as a Storyteller, with giving spirits Numina that mirror certain Facets of Shadow Gifts, especially if the spirit resonates with the theme of the Gift. The spirit of a library or a research spirit could definitely have a numen that mirrors <i>Sift the Sands</i> (Wisdom/Knowledge), for example. Or a secrecy spirit who has a numen that mirrors <i>Needle</i> (Cunning/Knowledge). It's not the Facets themselves, but it's not hard to see how they can be translated to suitable numina.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't those spirits possess a similar influence in those regards? I would simply have a spirit with a suitable influence carve the gifts into the Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4990-de_k47","name":"De_K47","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4990_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T01:29:37-07:00","id":582047,"title":"","content":"Something I thought lately about spirits and social maneuvers: shouldn't spirits have an hostile first impression of a Forsaken, and a good first impression of a Pure ? Of course I'm talking about default impression here, without any other factor than being a Forsaken or a Pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T06:46:29-07:00","id":582226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=582047#post582047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I thought lately about spirits and social maneuvers: shouldn't spirits have an hostile first impression of a Forsaken, and a good first impression of a Pure ? Of course I'm talking about default impression here, without any other factor than being a Forsaken or a Pure.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your rank is lower to the spirits, and you don't have a pack backing you up? Yes. With a pack it should be neutral usually, without taking into account stuff like messing with specific resonances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T18:33:01-07:00","id":585509,"title":"","content":"Social Manouvering shouldn't be used to EVERY social roll, that's an overuse of the rule. To begin with, in any interaction where things should be decided quick, you should use just a single roll. That probably should be also the answer when the other guy doesn't really care. If he didn't, he doesn't put ANY resistance, be it in the form of contest rolls or doors to begin with.<br /> <br /> Use Social Maneuvering just when the target have reason to not do what you want. If he doesn't care, so make a single roll or no roll at all.<br /> <br /> About spirits having Numina that mirror Gifts, just think first if you need, In the end, the spirit should have whatever Numina he needs. There are no relation between Numen and Facet, so that means both are free to have what they need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T21:29:18-07:00","id":585632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585509#post585509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Social Manouvering shouldn't be used to EVERY social roll, that's an overuse of the rule. To begin with, in any interaction where things should be decided quick, you should use just a single roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what Forcing Doors is for. If you need something from someone quickly, you either need to go to great lengths to earn their favor (increasing Impression) or pressure them into it (forcing doors).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585509#post585509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That probably should be also the answer when the other guy doesn't really care. If he didn't, he doesn't put ANY resistance, be it in the form of contest rolls or doors to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in that case you shouldn't even call for a roll, since there's no dramatic consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T21:51:16-07:00","id":585648,"title":"","content":"I do not agree, <b>Charlaquin</b>, second time this month - Apocalyspe is coming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Social Manuvering should be used in cases where the target is strongly opposed ( like most spirits in interactions with werewolves ). If we used this every time, it will go in to things like &quot;I want to buy a gun from him - Shopkeeper need to be Social Manuvered in to this&quot; - and a like nonsense.<br /> <br /> Until the target is not resisting coarsion, there is not need to Force the Doors - as the Target do not have putted those Door in first place. Or like the nerd is pick up by hot chick - it's his dreams come true, why would he resist her advnaces to get with him to bed?<br /> <br /> In mine game I used Social Manuvering when mine mage PCs wanted to coarsed the witch to letting them in to her inner sanctum. It <b>is</b> a big deal, if PCs are touched by Abyss. If she would not oposed the idea of them casually see them, I would not use Social Manuvering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-10-2015, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T22:36:05-07:00","id":585669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585648#post585648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not agree, <b>Charlaquin</b>, second time this month - Apocalyspe is coming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Haha no worries. It would be a little scary if you agreed with me on literally everything. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585648#post585648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Social Manuvering should be used in cases where the target is strongly opposed ( like most spirits in interactions with werewolves ). If we used this every time, it will go in to things like &quot;I want to buy a gun from him - Shopkeeper need to be Social Manuvered in to this&quot; - and a like nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you even call for a roll when trying to buy a gun from a shopkeeper? I mean, unless you're playing in a setting with strict gun control laws and you're essentially trying to convince this shopkeeper to break the law, but in that case I would consider that significant enough dramatic consequences that Social Maneuvering would be appropriate. The Social Maneuvering system is simply not designed to only come into play when the mark is strongly opposed to the person maneuvering. If it was, why would there be good and better impressions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585648#post585648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Until the target is not resisting coarsion, there is not need to Force the Doors - as the Target do not have putted those Door in first place. Or like the nerd is pick up by hot chick - it's his dreams come true, why would he resist her advnaces to get with him to bed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, if there's no resistance, why would you even need to roll dice at all?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585648#post585648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In mine game I used Social Manuvering when mine mage PCs wanted to coarsed the witch to letting them in to her inner sanctum. It <b>is</b> a big deal, if PCs are touched by Abyss. If she would not oposed the idea of them casually see them, I would not use Social Manuvering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, sure, but once again, if she's not opposed to the idea of them casually seeing her inner sanctum, why would you even use dice rolls to figure out if she'll let them see it? They want it, she's cool with it, you shouldn't even need to make a single roll to determine the outcome of that situation.<br /> <br /> Personally, I only call for rolls when two conditions are met:<br /> 1. There is a reasonable chance of the roll failing. If you don't have to roll dice to see if you tie your shoes correctly, why would you need to roll to buy something from a shopkeeper?<br /> 2. There are dramatic consequences for failure. Otherwise, why even bother rolling? Just adjudicate the results so we can move on to something more interesting.<br /> <br /> Now, I <i>have</i> seen quite a few people who don't use Social Maneuvering when the players need to convince a mark to do something (something worth rolling dice for) <i>right away</i>, because they feel the long intervals between rolls makes Social Maneuvering ill-suited to such a situation. To <i>that</i> I say, that's why the Impression and Forcing Doors rules exist. If you're in that much of a hurry to convince this character, you'd better make a damn good impression with him, or Force Doors to coerce him into it. 99% of the problems people have with the Social Maneuvering system can, in my opinion, be resolved by the ST being a bit more generous with Impressions, and the players being a lot more willing to Force Doors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-10-2015, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T22:41:27-07:00","id":585672,"title":"","content":"A nerd could still need Social Manouvering because he can suspect that's a ruse, and it's Big Bullying Time coming.<br /> <br /> That put aside, there are situations where you DO want a roll, but not Social Manouvering. That's when the other guy isn't really put into that to really resist, but you NEED to know his reaction. Sometimes the great speech is just a first act to acquire what you want. But sometimes you have to know about the speech by itself, and how much hearts you conquered at that very moment.<br /> <br /> In the same way sometimes you can reduce combat to a single roll, because you can't either deny it's relative relevance, nor think it deserves an entire scene, sometimes you need simpler rolls. I do understand the rationalle that you shouldn't ask a roll if it doesn't have drama, but sometimes you have moments that do have drama, but don't have enough complexity for Social Manouvering.<br /> <br /> Lets think about the PCs trying to sneack into a building. One of them tries first to talk the guard into this with some lye. This IS a dramatic roll. If he succedes, he can buy a passage for the PCs into the building. But if he fails, the guard isn't likely to listen to another try. In fact, the guard would probably suspect and reinforce security. If the guard isn't impressed, it isn't good enough. He will probably call for help.<br /> <br /> Such situation could call a Social Manouvering, but would hardly be the best option. It would bring too much variables to a simple question: he believes? Yes or not. There will be enough risks inside the building to take so much numbercrunching time with a guard, but enough drama in this for a roll be called. That should be a moment for a simple social roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T22:49:31-07:00","id":585673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585672#post585672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A nerd could still need Social Manouvering because he can suspect that's a ruse, and it's Big Bullying Time coming.<br /> <br /> That put aside, there are situations where you DO want a roll, but not Social Manouvering. That's when the other guy isn't really put into that to really resist, but you NEED to know his reaction. Sometimes the great speech is just a first act to acquire what you want. But sometimes you have to know about the speech by itself, and how much hearts you conquered at that very moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, like when you're using a social action to do something that doesn't involve convincing another character to do something. Maybe when you're trying to inspire someone, or rally a crowd, or figure out whether or not someone is lying, or what have you. Social Maneuvering is for getting other characters to do what you want, if that's not the goal of your social action, then it goes without saying Social Maneuvering wouldn't be the appropriate way to resolve that action.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585672#post585672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the same way sometimes you can reduce combat to a single roll, because you can't either deny it's relative relevance, nor think it deserves an entire scene, sometimes you need simpler rolls. I do understand the rationalle that you shouldn't ask a roll if it doesn't have drama, but sometimes you have moments that do have drama, but don't have enough complexity for Social Manouvering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, what I'm saying is, that's exactly what the Forcing Doors rules are for.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585672#post585672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets think about the PCs trying to sneack into a building. One of them tries first to talk the guard into this with some lye. This IS a dramatic roll. If he succedes, he can buy a passage for the PCs into the building. But if he fails, the guard isn't likely to listen to another try. In fact, the guard would probably suspect and reinforce security. If the guard isn't impressed, it isn't good enough. He will probably call for help.</div> </div> </div> </div>That definitely sounds like a Forcing Doors roll to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585672#post585672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such situation could call a Social Manouvering, but would hardly be the best option. It would bring too much variables to a simple question: he believes? Yes or not. There will be enough risks inside the building to take so much numbercrunching time with a guard, but enough drama in this for a roll be called. That should be a moment for a simple social roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, there's not really any number crunching involved in Social Maneuvering. You roll your dice pool, if you get one or more successes you open a Door. Then you have to wait a duration (based on Impression) before you can try again. If you need something in a hurry, you can use soft leverage and other techniques to try to raise the impression. If you need a single-roll resolution, Force Doors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-10-2015, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T03:58:07-07:00","id":585828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585669#post585669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I only call for rolls when two conditions are met:<br /> 1. There is a reasonable chance of the roll failing. If you don't have to roll dice to see if you tie your shoes correctly, why would you need to roll to buy something from a shopkeeper?<br /> 2. There are dramatic consequences for failure. Otherwise, why even bother rolling? Just adjudicate the results so we can move on to something more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>As it seems, we agree on major points. Maybe mine reading of English on morning was just low then and that I thought you do not agree with me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585669#post585669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I <i>have</i> seen quite a few people who don't use Social Maneuvering when the players need to convince a mark to do something (something worth rolling dice for) <i>right away</i>, because they feel the long intervals between rolls makes Social Maneuvering ill-suited to such a situation. To <i>that</i> I say, that's why the Impression and Forcing Doors rules exist. If you're in that much of a hurry to convince this character, you'd better make a damn good impression with him, or Force Doors to coerce him into it. 99% of the problems people have with the Social Maneuvering system can, in my opinion, be resolved by the ST being a bit more generous with Impressions, and the players being a lot more willing to Force Doors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is where i clearly have objection - for me, if Goal the player want to make is resolved in the same scene ( like &quot;give me the Artifact you hold in hand!&quot; ) using Social Maneuvering is too much and not totally counter-thematic to the character. You are not making prepared speeches and nice environment to slowly influence the Target - you are using your abilities more like fighting skills - you &quot;shoot&quot; with Persuasion or Intimidation for quick response. I <i>could</i> consider using the SM system to make NPC divarge from his long term Aspirations or basic characters goals ( like protecting the daughter or finally becoming Hierarch of the city ), but still would more think that decisions made &quot;in the heat of the moment&quot; need to use normal Social Skills roles, just like you would fire a gun or attack with your fists him. Also, it makes game much more dynamic than trying every single time count Doors and assume Impressions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-10-2015, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T05:54:17-07:00","id":585936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585828#post585828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is where i clearly have objection - for me, if Goal the player want to make is resolved in the same scene ( like &quot;give me the Artifact you hold in hand!&quot; ) using Social Maneuvering is too much and not totally counter-thematic to the character. You are not making prepared speeches and nice environment to slowly influence the Target - you are using your abilities more like fighting skills - you &quot;shoot&quot; with Persuasion or Intimidation for quick response. I <i>could</i> consider using the SM system to make NPC divarge from his long term Aspirations or basic characters goals ( like protecting the daughter or finally becoming Hierarch of the city ), but still would more think that decisions made &quot;in the heat of the moment&quot; need to use normal Social Skills roles, just like you would fire a gun or attack with your fists him. Also, it makes game much more dynamic than trying every single time count Doors and assume Impressions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, what you're describing here is a situation where you would want to use a Forcing Doors roll. One roll, you get enough successes, you get the person to do what you want. You don't get enough successes, you don't get them to do what you want. I'm not saying single-roll social actions are never called for. I'm saying there is a rules system within the Social Maneuvering mechanics for single-roll actions. It's called Forcing Doors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T06:01:16-07:00","id":585963,"title":"","content":"But this action is one stand - in your interpretation you Force Door or not. Either way it's ended and Social Maneuvering would not be reattempted later ( because your enemy get away with Artifact, for example ). You cannot return to it and try again. It's all or nothing, with resolution in this scene.<br /> <br /> Other question in topic - Once using Influence of spirits is still Social Maneuvering?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T06:09:08-07:00","id":585971,"title":"","content":"Remember that Argument, Carousing, Fast-talk and Interrogation are sample simple action in the book...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T06:15:31-07:00","id":585975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585963#post585963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this action is one stand - in your interpretation you Force Door or not. Either way it's ended and Social Maneuvering would not be reattempted later ( because your enemy get away with Artifact, for example ). You cannot return to it and try again. It's all or nothing, with resolution in this scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly how Forcing Doors works. You make one single roll, pass or fail. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585963#post585963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other question in topic - Once using Influence of spirits is still Social Maneuvering?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like convincing a spirit to use their Influences to help you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T06:17:48-07:00","id":585977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585971#post585971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that Argument, Carousing, Fast-talk and Interrogation are sample simple action in the book...</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, so those determine what dice pools to use based on your approach.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Nice profile picture by the way, I love Kaori Yuki so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T06:37:57-07:00","id":585994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585977#post585977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, so those determine what dice pools to use based on your approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nowhere in GMC, VtR2 or WtF2 is mentionned that these suggested actions must be used in SM. They have immediate result of their own, even if I can see them used in SM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585977#post585977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: Nice profile picture by the way, I love Kaori Yuki so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not usually a manga guy, but I loved Angel Sanctuary on first sight <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T07:13:08-07:00","id":586060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585994#post585994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nowhere in GMC, VtR2 or WtF2 is mentionned that these suggested actions must be used in SM. They have immediate result of their own, even if I can see them used in SM.</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure. There's no rule that says you have to use them with Social Maneuvering, I just find Social Maneuvering to be the best system for resolving actions where the goal is to get another character to do something. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=585994#post585994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not usually a manga guy, but I loved Angel Sanctuary on first sight <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I got into her work through the Cain Saga/Godchild. Angel Sanctuary is fantastic though, and a great inspirational resource for God Machine and Demon games!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T07:17:50-07:00","id":586063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=586060#post586060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For sure. There's no rule that says you have to use them with Social Maneuvering, I just find Social Maneuvering to be the best system for resolving actions where the goal is to get another character to do something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, my bad, thought the debate was on how it was meant to be, not your preference <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=586060#post586060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got into her work through the Cain Saga/Godchild. Angel Sanctuary is fantastic though, and a great inspirational resource for God Machine and Demon games!</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, I was surprised not to see it in the DtD references<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T08:10:39-07:00","id":586085,"title":"","content":"Charlaquin, thanks for hammering on Forcing Doors: Rereading the Social Maneuvering section with an eye towards Forcing Doors and how that's different from Hard Leverage made it all finally click into place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T08:26:41-07:00","id":586139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=586085#post586085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charlaquin, thanks for hammering on Forcing Doors: Rereading the Social Maneuvering section with an eye towards Forcing Doors and how that's different from Hard Leverage made it all finally click into place.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> sorry if I'm coming off as overzealous about it, I definitely don't mean to force anyone to play the game my way. I just think the Forcing Doors mechanics are often overlooked, because the way they're presented makes them look like something you'd almost never want to use. I see them more as the Social Maneuvering system's version of Down and Dirty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T08:35:58-07:00","id":586146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=586139#post586139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No problem <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> sorry if I'm coming off as overzealous about it, I definitely don't mean to force anyone to play the game my way. I just think the Forcing Doors mechanics are often overlooked, because the way they're presented makes them look like something you'd almost never want to use. I see them more as the Social Maneuvering system's version of Down and Dirty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I've been overlooking the Social Maneuvering system entirely though just because I didn't get it. I messed around once with a pack convincing a group of disease spirits to let the medicine and health spirits back into a hospital, but wasn't sure that I was doing things correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T08:42:50-07:00","id":586153,"title":"","content":"Makes sense. For me it clicked right away, because it added what I felt was some much-needed structure to the process of resolving social actions with dice rolls, in a way that didn't just feel like physical combat. Anything I can do to help you grok the system better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T08:50:45-07:00","id":586158,"title":"","content":"Maybe me, I still have problems with Social Maneuvering - but in two days we will have game session opened on this witch NPC I mentioned before and players will try to convince her. Maybe after this I will have more thoughts about.<br /> <br /> For now, a small subtopic - <b>Is typical &quot;<i>dear spirits, heal me cause I'm dying from wounds!</i>&quot; the Social Maneuvering roll or just standard persuasion quick check?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-10-2015, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T08:53:45-07:00","id":586161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=586153#post586153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes sense. For me it clicked right away, because it added what I felt was some much-needed structure to the process of resolving social actions with dice rolls, in a way that didn't just feel like physical combat. Anything I can do to help you grok the system better?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly what I need to do is just practice it with a variety of scenarios. My biggest issue originally was just deciding whether or not it was appropriate to use it. My problem was always related to the long-term aspect of it -- and worrying that my players would balk at it. Now that I'm more confident about how to decide when it's appropriate, I think I can overcome the latter issue and just break it out more often.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T09:55:13-07:00","id":586224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=586158#post586158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe me, I still have problems with Social Maneuvering - but in two days we will have game session opened on this witch NPC I mentioned before and players will try to convince her. Maybe after this I will have more thoughts about.<br /> <br /> For now, a small subtopic - <b>Is typical &quot;<i>dear spirits, heal me cause I'm dying from wounds!</i>&quot; the Social Maneuvering roll or just standard persuasion quick check?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, Social Maneuvering is never required if you don't want to use it. But for a situation like that, I would use Social Maneuvering because you are trying to convince another character (the spirit) to do something (heal you).<br /> <br /> Since you're seriously injured, this is obviously an urgent matter and you don't have time to slowly work to make a spirit like you. Your best option would be to call upon a spirit you already have a positive relationship with, like your pack's totem. That might not require any roll, or it might be a few quick rolls over a couple of turns at a Perfect Impression.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if no allied spirits are available to help, you'll need to express how urgent the situation is to what ever random spirit you're trying to convince. Telling them &quot;I need healing RIGHT NOW, are you going to help me or not?&quot; would be a Forcing Doors roll.<br /> <br /> Forcing Doors is just a single roll (of what ever dice pool you deem appropriate) with a penalty equal to the Mark's Doors. On a successful roll the Mark does what you want, on a failed roll they don't, and you can't try again. It's almost identical to a standard non-social-maneuvering Social Roll, the only way it really interacts with the SM system is that the penalty is based on the target's Doors (i.e. The lower of their Resolve or Composure, with potential additional penalties if you're asking a lot of them.)<br /> <br /> Though, remember, a Spirit can't offer services without being given proper <i>Gartha</i> first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-10-2015, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:39:01-07:00","id":586297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=586224#post586224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forcing Doors is just a single roll (of what ever dice pool you deem appropriate) with a penalty equal to the Mark's Doors. On a successful roll the Mark does what you want, on a failed roll they don't, and you can't try again. It's almost identical to a standard non-social-maneuvering Social Roll, the only way it really interacts with the SM system is that the penalty is based on the target's Doors (i.e. The lower of their Resolve or Composure, with potential additional penalties if you're asking a lot of them.)<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I really think this is the point here. I think people are getting hung up on the phrase 'Use Social Manuevering', the situations there talking about, they are using Forcing Doors (assuming they use the targets Resolve or Composure to determine the success)(and yeah, either as a Resistance or number of Doors, that just changes the odds not really the idea) they just don't call it Social Manuevering or think of it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T12:07:11-07:00","id":586312,"title":"","content":"Another metaphor:<br /> <br /> Forcing Doors is to Social Maneuvering as Down &amp; Dirty is to Physical Combat.<br /> <br /> That one die roll <i>is</i> Forcing Doors. Heck, if you don't want to play with the Social Maneuvering system as it stands, just steal the modifiers to the number of doors, and use those as guidelines for bonuses and penalties to social rolls.<br /> <br /> So convincing someone to do something would be a Presence + Persuasion - Resolve roll, where you'd get a penalty if it opposes their Virtue or one of their Aspirations, and would be impossible if they suspected you were leading them on or lying to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T12:14:07-07:00","id":586316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=586312#post586312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another metaphor:<br /> <br /> Forcing Doors is to Social Maneuvering as Down &amp; Dirty is to Physical Combat.<br /> <br /> That one die roll <i>is</i> Forcing Doors. Heck, if you don't want to play with the Social Maneuvering system as it stands, just steal the modifiers to the number of doors, and use those as guidelines for bonuses and penalties to social rolls.<br /> <br /> So convincing someone to do something would be a Presence + Persuasion - Resolve roll, where you'd get a penalty if it opposes their Virtue or one of their Aspirations, and would be impossible if they suspected you were leading them on or lying to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is what I've been trying to say. You said it better though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T12:34:19-07:00","id":586353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=586316#post586316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, this is what I've been trying to say. You said it better though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly; good ideas sometimes need to be made explicit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T12:35:21-07:00","id":586354,"title":"","content":"I get it, and surely Soial Maneuvering was more of an issue to understand than it should be to use. I still think that sometimes there are no reason to use even one Door, but in that I digress. Thanks Charlaquin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T13:31:26-07:00","id":586415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=586312#post586312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another metaphor:<br /> <br /> Forcing Doors is to Social Maneuvering as Down &amp; Dirty is to Physical Combat.<br /> <br /> That one die roll <i>is</i> Forcing Doors. Heck, if you don't want to play with the Social Maneuvering system as it stands, just steal the modifiers to the number of doors, and use those as guidelines for bonuses and penalties to social rolls.<br /> <br /> So convincing someone to do something would be a Presence + Persuasion - Resolve roll, where you'd get a penalty if it opposes their Virtue or one of their Aspirations, and would be impossible if they suspected you were leading them on or lying to them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that's what I meant too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T03:37:15-07:00","id":586942,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly secure that summoning a spirit and binding it to the material side of the gauntlet, so it bleeds essence over time in order to demand a task from it is Forcing Doors with Hard Leverage (Also, ironically, apparently a breaking point towards Flesh.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T09:18:42-07:00","id":587183,"title":"","content":"It isn't a Breaking Point for the Spirit itself, so isn't covered by Social Maneuvering rules as far as I remember right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T09:31:13-07:00","id":587189,"title":"","content":"Spirits don't suffer breaking points. As far as it being covered by rules?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>W:tF, Second Edition pg 164</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">To make things easier for the persuading character, he can apply Hard Leverage \u2014 a catch-all euphemism for threats, intimidation, drugging, blackmail, and other heavy-handed forms of coercion. If the persuader uses a form of Hard Leverage, it\u2019s a breaking point towards Flesh. Against humans Hard Leverage removes one Door if the character\u2019s Harmony is 8 or more; used on spirits remove one Door if the character\u2019s Harmony is 2 or less. Otherwise, it removes two Doors. Hard Leverage can only be used in conjunction with forcing Doors; remove the Doors before rolling for the character\u2019s approach.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T11:23:39-07:00","id":587267,"title":"","content":"Shame on me, I was talking bullshit on the last one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T23:27:47-07:00","id":592371,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking I'm probably going to use a spirit's Rank as its Doors rating. Keeps the paperwork to a minimum, and keeps the godlike ones within the realm of actually being influenced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T23:56:55-07:00","id":592377,"title":"","content":"I prefer using the lower of Finesse or Resistance. Godlike beings shouldn't be easily swayed and should require a lot of time to rouse to your side. I don't picture rank 4 or 5 Spirits being all that easy to intimidate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T07:58:18-07:00","id":592620,"title":"","content":"I'd say it depends on your desired difficulty level and avoiding tedious rolling. You have to admit that sometimes the speed of your Storytelling is making the game slower than t really has to be. Communication is key. This hobby is equal parts imagination and socializing. I don't mean to sound like Captain Obvious, but the power of the obvious shouldn't be underestimated. It's not even that complicated. Just imagine this:<br /> <br /> ST: &quot;Am I going too slow? Do you think we should ditch Social Maneuvering this time?&quot;<br /> P1: &quot;Yeah. We've been rolling for half an hour just to get into the shady night club, and the dice seem to be in a bad mood today.&quot;<br /> P2: &quot;Agreed. Let's leave SM for the scenes where we interrogate the vampire mafioso's more important henchmen.&quot;<br /> ST: &quot;Got it. I'll be on the look out for this kind of problem in the future.&quot;<br /> <br /> And then they had fun.<br /> <br /> As for more concrete rules, I suggest this: the base number of Doors required to convince an ephemeral being to do something is equal to its Rank. If you want to make that harder, the base number of Doors is equal to Resistance + Rank/2 round up. Spirits don't have Virtue or Vice, but you may treat a Spirit's Virtue as &quot;Increase Rank&quot; and Vice as &quot;Spread Influence&quot;. For ghosts, Virtue and Vice in Social Maneuvering are inverted: going against their Vice adds one Door, but taking advantage of their Virtue moves your Impression one step up. For Angels, those Traits work the same as with a human. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T08:39:15-07:00","id":592656,"title":"","content":"Base number of Doors for spirits should be Resistance, just that. Rank is too low, as is too wyld and unnecessary to consider Power or Finesse.<br /> <br /> Powerful beings shouldn't be easily swayed, and no, it isn't make it too hard. In the end, more Doors is just make for more scenes before the end of the S-M.<br /> <br /> That aside, I think we already discussed it to length. S-M is enough for its proposed intent. Forcing Doors cover quick uses, not using it at all cover any situation where you don't see reason to roll dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T09:55:23-07:00","id":592830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=592620#post592620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say it depends on your desired difficulty level and avoiding tedious rolling. You have to admit that sometimes the speed of your Storytelling is making the game slower than t really has to be. Communication is key. This hobby is equal parts imagination and socializing. I don't mean to sound like Captain Obvious, but the power of the obvious shouldn't be underestimated. It's not even that complicated. Just imagine this:<br /> <br /> ST: &quot;Am I going too slow? Do you think we should ditch Social Maneuvering this time?&quot;<br /> P1: &quot;Yeah. We've been rolling for half an hour just to get into the shady night club, and the dice seem to be in a bad mood today.&quot;<br /> P2: &quot;Agreed. Let's leave SM for the scenes where we interrogate the vampire mafioso's more important henchmen.&quot;<br /> ST: &quot;Got it. I'll be on the look out for this kind of problem in the future.&quot;<br /> <br /> And then they had fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did they decide to resolve that action with a single roll, or to adjudicate the results without dice? If the former, they're actually still using Social Maneuvering - that's what Forcing Doors is. If the latter, that's a totally reasonable call, no need to bring dice into it if the group doesn't find the potential consequences of failing the action interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=592620#post592620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for more concrete rules, I suggest this: the base number of Doors required to convince an ephemeral being to do something is equal to its Rank. If you want to make that harder, the base number of Doors is equal to Resistance + Rank/2 round up. Spirits don't have Virtue or Vice, but you may treat a Spirit's Virtue as &quot;Increase Rank&quot; and Vice as &quot;Spread Influence&quot;. For ghosts, Virtue and Vice in Social Maneuvering are inverted: going against their Vice adds one Door, but taking advantage of their Virtue moves your Impression one step up. For Angels, those Traits work the same as with a human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Resistance really is the best trait to use for number of Doors, but I like your ideas for Virtues and Vices. I might use those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T14:09:13-07:00","id":593133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/558701-spirit-doors?p=592830#post592830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did they decide to resolve that action with a single roll, or to adjudicate the results without dice? If the former, they're actually still using Social Maneuvering - that's what Forcing Doors is. If the latter, that's a totally reasonable call, no need to bring dice into it if the group doesn't find the potential consequences of failing the action interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think Resistance really is the best trait to use for number of Doors, but I like your ideas for Virtues and Vices. I might use those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the compliment! It means a lot to me when I get such praise, especially when it's from prominent users like you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for your question, it is the latter. No dice rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}